1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:08,228
When engineers are working, especially on existing applications, you sometimes find they're spending less than an hour of their day actually writing code.

2
00:00:08,846 --> 00:00:09,920
Most engineers know this.

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,960
Unless you have the privilege of building your own unique thing, you're interacting with lots of people.

4
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,480
There is so much happening.

5
00:00:16,782 --> 00:00:20,560
Coordination tax, testing tax, translation tax.

6
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:35,840
And we really wanted to build a methodology that was backed by software and best practices that would bring all of that together, that would drive real appreciable outcomes so you could build things, not code, but outcomes, fast.

7
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:40,000
Know how to measure them, and we've seen incredible results.

8
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:45,316
Hey everyone, welcome to the Humans in the Loop podcast.

9
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:49,120
I'm your host, Chris Shea, a solutions architect at Amazon Web Services.

10
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:56,676
Today's episode is all about AI DLC, the AI-driven development lifecycle and how it's changing the pace at which developers can innovate.

11
00:00:57,422 --> 00:01:01,280
Joining me today is Shao Nandi, VP of Technology at Amazon Web Services.

12
00:01:01,678 --> 00:01:05,732
And I'm also joined by Anupam Mishra, Director of AI Engineering at AWS.

13
00:01:06,318 --> 00:01:07,200
Thanks for joining me on the show.

14
00:01:07,534 --> 00:01:08,240
Thank you for having us.

15
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:08,996
Thanks for having us.

16
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,880
Shao, I think a great place to start would tell me a little bit about your background, your current role, and the path that brought you here.

17
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,280
Yeah, look, I lead our field engineering team.

18
00:01:17,454 --> 00:01:24,160
So our solution architects, our customer solutions managers worldwide, spent a lot of time talking with customers with AI.

19
00:01:24,366 --> 00:01:26,404
But how I got here, it's a checkered journey.

20
